From 0a88590ac7febcf3c7a5c933199a2a9c0d41c9e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:27:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/29] droidian: beyond2lte: one full defconfig, ABOX firmware
 built in

Merge the Droidian configuration fragments into the device defconfig and
stop applying fragments at build time (KERNEL_CONFIG_USE_FRAGMENTS = 0), so
the configuration that boots is a single reviewable file.

Build the ABOX firmware into the kernel (CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE, files in
firmware/ copied from the phone's vendor partition, not part of the tree),
and enable what the Droidian userspace needs: binderfs with the Halium
binder devices, Bluetooth RFCOMM/BNEP/HIDP, VT console, user and IPC
namespaces, BTF for the extra modules.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
